# `zfetch`, a C program on libposix sockets, against the host-side test server
# (N4; `make test-net-posix`, which turns @PORT@ and the @SUM...@ checksums
# into numbers, as `make test-net-fetch` does). The program is /bin/zfetch of
# the disk, run through the broker; the shell gives it a connection to the host
# and port of the URL on its line (ADR-0224 item 2) at the NET slot.
! panicked
! first process ended
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
# The lease takes a few hundred milliseconds under TCG.
> sleep 3\r
< \r\n~>
# The same page as `fetch`, byte for byte, by address.
> zfetch http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/\r
< Zoraya test page

< fetched over HTTP, byte for byte

< \r\n~>
# Each framing, by checksum: the numbers `fetch --sum` is compared with.
> zfetch --sum http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/pattern/1000000\r
< 1000000 bytes fnv1a @SUM1M@ in
< \r\n~>
> zfetch --sum http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/close/70000\r
< 70000 bytes fnv1a @SUM70K@ in
< \r\n~>
# By name: getaddrinfo asks netd (net.hosts gives test.zoraya), and connect
# goes by the name it came from (INV-0225-2).
> zfetch --sum http://test.zoraya:@PORT@/chunked/300000\r
< 300000 bytes fnv1a @SUM300K@ in
< \r\n~>
# More than the rings and the socket buffers hold.
> zfetch --sum http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/pattern/4000000\r
< 4000000 bytes fnv1a @SUM4M@ in
< \r\n~>
# What goes wrong is said, and the exit status is 1.
> zfetch http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/status/404\r
< zfetch: http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/status/404: HTTP 404
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< \r\nexit status 1
< \r\n~>
> zfetch http://10.0.2.2:1/\r
< Connection refused
< \r\n~>
# A server that closes after the head: the page is cut, and the program says so.
> zfetch --sum http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/reset\r
< the connection closed before the end of the page
< \r\n~>
# A URL from a value does not designate: the line is refused before it runs.
> set u http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/\r
< \r\n~>
> zfetch $u\r
< from a value, outside the line's network grants
< \r\n~>
# Without the grant (INV-0225-1): the socket is made, and connect is refused.
> posixrun -m /bin=/bin:ro -m /home=/home -C /home /bin/zfetch http://10.0.2.2:@PORT@/\r
< zfetch: 10.0.2.2: Permission denied
< posixrun: exit 1
< \r\n~>
x power off
> poweroff\r
